SUMMARY:Lunar-pole light window · Valle de Santiago maars
LOCATION:20.1878, -101.3692
GEO:20.18776;-101.36915
DESCRIPTION:Sun 0–7° above the horizon (morning\, azimuth 115°→118°)
 : the light of the lunar south pole. Analog of: Leibnitz Beta Plateau\, Sh
 ackleton Connecting Ridge\, Haworth. Test rover vision\, EVA lighting and 
 shadow navigation. Brief: data/processed/briefs/earth_mx_valle_santiago.md
END:VEVENT
